cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use corrosim in your research, please cite it as below."
title: corrosim
abstract: >-
  Automated screening of green corrosion inhibitors: from a molecule (name or
  SMILES) and a metal, it computes DFT/QM reactivity descriptors, a Monte Carlo
  adsorption estimate, and a Brownian-dynamics metal-oxygen RDF, then ranks the
  candidates and emits a self-contained HTML report.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Georgiev
    given-names: Branimir
repository-code: "https://github.com/braboj/corrosim"
url: "https://github.com/braboj/corrosim"
license: MIT
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-07-20
keywords:
  - corrosion inhibitor
  - green chemistry
  - DFT
  - Monte Carlo
  - molecular dynamics
  - computational screening

